{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/624778-retainers-and-status","id":624778,"title":"Retainers and Status?","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Vampire: The Requiem"],"posts":[{"date":"2015-08-12T17:34:47-07:00","id":624778,"title":"Retainers and Status?","content":"Personally I love the streamlining done for second edition VtR (and most of what I've seen in 2nd ed too). But my question is about the Retainers merit. The classic image is of Vampires with their fingers in all the mortals' pies, whether through retainers or allies (Invictus or Carthian respectively for perks). In first ed, it was easy enough to have retainers that were part of an institution to have status in that, (retainer is a cop, doctor, etc) <br /> While I like the ease of use for retainers in 2nd ed, but I'm not sure how to go about having retainers/ghouls with status. <br /> <br /> the first option I'm leaning to is simply having retainers have status equal to their dots in what ever institution they are a part of. Example: 3 dot retainer that's a cop dice pool of 6 for investigation draws and status three in the Police. <br /> <br /> the second option, which is more limiting, is requiring retainers to be bought for skills and then other retainers for status. Note: retainers get draws equal to their dots except for one pool. Status adds to any social draw with that group. so the rationale behind this is that the Status dice pool IS the dice pool the retainer is doubling. But then the retainer is nothing but a status draw. <br /> <br /> Which was the more intended version? which do you think is better?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7269-afrodave","name":"afrodave","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-12T18:22:23-07:00","id":624859,"title":"","content":"You could model it off of the Attache merit for the Invictus. It gives your Retainer merit dots equal to your Invictus Status which can be accessed through them. I might suggest making it a 1 or 2 dot merit which gives your retainer some level of tangible status in an organization that might be helpful, but I'd probably keep it around 3 or something for a vampire's ghoul retainer. Ghouls can be noticeable the higher up they are, and characters in top levels of establishments are probably busy enough that you wouldn't model them with retainer rules.<br /> <br /> You could maybe look at Mentor rules for inspiration on how to handle a really connected NPC which has been put under your thrall, but you might have to rework the drawback.<br /> <br /> My personal preference is to have social merits that a retainer might have be incidental rather than purchased, but I can see why people might want rules for it.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I am no longer participating in the community. Please do not contact me about my previous work.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/159-leetsepeak","name":"Leetsepeak","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4259"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-12T18:37:00-07:00","id":624897,"title":"","content":"For me, the question is what exactly you're hoping to get out of this status.<br /> <br /> Contacts or Allies might make more sense, applied to the retainer.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1692-maina","name":"Maina","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1692_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"724"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-13T02:07:02-07:00","id":625223,"title":"","content":"Intended version? My guess would be that if the vampire has draw in an organization, they buy status, contacts, and allies, in which case, with allies or status, they can have members of that organization do things for them, and whether they got that pull through bribery, extortion, dominate, or blood bonding, is unimportant. <br /> <br /> You may want to take a look at Damnation City for its optional system for vampires controlling people or things.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/391-stsword","name":"StSword","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar391_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1635"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-13T02:40:34-07:00","id":625255,"title":"","content":"Not all servants and blood thralls are Retainers. Not all Retainers are Allies and Contacts, or even Herd and Staff. Its intended that youhave to buy each separately, even if its all through one person.<br /> <br /> I also think that you are misunderstanding what Status represents. Yes, it gives a social bonus (which is different from a dice pool, and a minor aspect) but the big draw is actually access to the organization's resources and ability to block other people's merits. Each merit is highly distinct in what it can do. Well, except Allies/Contacts, that has mucho overlap. But the rest are distinct.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2102-mcn","name":"MCN","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2102_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3479"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-13T04:27:40-07:00","id":625296,"title":"","content":"Another way to put what <b>MCN</b> said: the Merit is a mechanical function, not a description. And you need Merits to determine what you can actually do.<br /> <br /> Retainers, as Merits, are for you to have a sidekick of sorts with clear dice pools for rolls.<br /> <br /> Status is your pull into an organization.<br /> <br /> You want a Ghoul of yours to be in the police? YOU buy Retainer AND Status (Police). Maybe a <b>Condition: Status by Proxy</b> to represent that both benefits and drawbacks come to your Retainer instead of to yourself.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-13T05:22:59-07:00","id":625316,"title":"","content":"Conversely, if you have a doctor &quot;retainer&quot; that you've recruited and you just want access to drugs or bagged blood, but you're not interested in having the doc make medicine rolls? Then you can just ignore buying the Retainer merit in the first place and invest in Allies or Status (both could work).<br /> <br /> This way, you can pick and choose what mechanics you care about. Sure, its a bit expensive EXP wise, but that's an OOC resource, plus there's Sanctity of Merits if something happens to the doc.<br /> <br /> If you feel its too expensive, talk to the ST to make a merit that combines the two merits into one purchase. There's several merits that combine a few of the benefits. &quot;Your Library is also your Herd.&quot; Things like that. <br /> <br /> Personally, I don't know of a good way to combine everything, because really, when you get down to it, too much depends on the relationship you have with the person. A police thrall could serve as a Retainer, an Ally, a Contact, part of your Herd, a Mentor, and part of a Library, all in one. Its hard to pick and choose. Combining several merits into one just because we're talking about a single person can get rather overpowered really fast. May as well just make one social merit, since we can justify mixing them all together.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2102-mcn","name":"MCN","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2102_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3479"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-13T06:56:16-07:00","id":625411,"title":"","content":"Yes, well... the Individual who is a Retainer, an Ally, a Contact, part of your Herd, a Mentor, has status in an organization, and is part of a Library, all in one, is also a very prime target as well... If you have invested so much into this one person, it only follows that others will also be interested in this one person. I am a big proponent for splitting social functions amongst many for this very reason. It is <i><b>MUCH </b></i>harder to screw with a person's assets if they are diverse, rather than being rolled into one.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i><span style=\"font-family:Times New Roman\"><span style=\"font-family:Times New Roman\">The problem with defending the purity of the English language is that English is about as pure as a cribhouse whore. We don't just borrow words; on occasion, English has pursued other languages down alleyways to beat them unconscious and rifle their pockets for new vocabulary. - James. D. Nicoll</span></span></i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/540-tymeaus-jalynsfein","name":"Tymeaus Jalynsfein","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"869"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-13T09:36:39-07:00","id":625631,"title":"","content":"Thanks for the input guys, I think I like the feel that Leetspeak was going for. <br /> Merit: <br /> Connected Kindred (One dot) (Prerequisite City Status 1)<br /> You've been in the City, you know who's who. Most importantly, you know how to get the best quality retainers. Each of your retainers is someone important in their own private circle. Each of your retainers has dots in status in one mortal institution equal to your City Status.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7269-afrodave","name":"afrodave","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}